<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Authored for Geldar (0352 and 0370). [AUTH] Not upstream.
  Password hashes are NOT in git. Each hash is read from the container environment with from_env:
  GELDAR_CH_WRITER_SHA256, GELDAR_CH_READER_SHA256 and GELDAR_CH_SIGNOZ_ADMIN_SHA256 (THREE hashes; the last is used only in
   the retention window but is required while geldar_signoz_admin is defined here). Compose loads them from the node-only env file
  /mnt/nvme/geldar-telemetry/secrets/ch-hashes.env (README, "Password hashes"). from_env in config is [INF, unverified on 25.12.5].
  Limits from 0352: writer max_memory_usage 2 GB, max_threads 4, max_execution_time 60, max_insert_threads 2.
  Reader limits follow 0352 (Read path, B): readonly 2, 1 GB, max_execution_time 30, max_result_rows 100000 with break,
  SELECT grants on the signoz_* databases. Threads 4 are [AUTH]. The per-hour read quota of 0352 is NOT set here: 0352 gives no value [UNV].
  The grants use the XML users grants element [INF, unverified on 25.12.5]. geldar_writer is granted the six signoz_* databases the
  migrator creates (signoz_analytics, signoz_logs, signoz_metadata, signoz_meter, signoz_metrics, signoz_traces). geldar_reader is
  granted SELECT on signoz_traces, signoz_logs, signoz_metrics and signoz_metadata only; it has NO grant on signoz_meter or
  signoz_analytics (left as is; a gap to decide, not changed here).
  default: kept because the cluster entry in cluster.xml has no user (README unverified list). Its grants are in the default block.
  Networks for default are loopback only (127.0.0.1, ::1). Both <networks> and each <ip> carry replace="replace" so the stock ::/0
  is not kept by the merge [INF, unverified on 25.12.5; README item 21]. access_management and named_collection_control are removed from default explicitly in the default block, because the stock config sets them.
  Nothing is published. Widen only if the scratch run shows ON CLUSTER refused.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <profiles>
        <geldar_writer>
            <max_memory_usage>2000000000</max_memory_usage>
            <max_threads>4</max_threads>
            <max_execution_time>60</max_execution_time>
            <max_insert_threads>2</max_insert_threads>
            <load_balancing>in_order</load_balancing>
            <log_queries>1</log_queries>
        </geldar_writer>
        <geldar_reader>
            <readonly>2</readonly>
            <max_memory_usage>1000000000</max_memory_usage>
            <max_threads>4</max_threads>
            <max_execution_time>30</max_execution_time>
            <max_result_rows>100000</max_result_rows>
            <result_overflow_mode>break</result_overflow_mode>
            <load_balancing>in_order</load_balancing>
        </geldar_reader>
        <!-- [AUTH] Retention window only (D3). Not readonly: ALTER ... MODIFY TTL is DDL. 600 s because the ALTER on a large table
             can take longer than the reader's 30 s [UNV]. -->
        <geldar_signoz_admin>
            <readonly>0</readonly>
            <max_memory_usage>2000000000</max_memory_usage>
            <max_threads>4</max_threads>
            <max_execution_time>600</max_execution_time>
            <load_balancing>in_order</load_balancing>
        </geldar_signoz_admin>
    </profiles>
    <users>
        <default>
            <password></password>
            <networks replace="replace">
                <ip replace="replace">127.0.0.1</ip>
                <ip replace="replace">::1</ip>
            </networks>
            <profile>default</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <!-- [AUTH] The stock config sets access_management and named_collection_control on default (image users.xml, lines 89
                 and 92). They must be removed here because ClickHouse refuses explicit <grants> next to any access-control key
                 (Code 347, "Any other access control settings can't be specified with grants"). show_named_collections and
                 show_named_collections_secrets are removed too, as belt and braces. Effect: default can no longer manage access or
                 named collections. ClickHouse starts on this config (scratch report8). -->
            <access_management remove="remove"/>
            <named_collection_control remove="remove"/>
            <show_named_collections remove="remove"/>
            <show_named_collections_secrets remove="remove"/>
            <!-- [AUTH] default exists because the cluster entry in cluster.xml has no <user>, so Distributed tables and
                 clusterAllReplicas reach the shard as default. Its grants are limited to what that needs: SELECT and INSERT on the
                 six signoz_* databases and SELECT on system.*. Nothing else: no SOURCES, SYSTEM, FILE, URL, S3, REMOTE, ALTER,
                 CREATE, DROP, TABLE ENGINE or access management. Distributed DDL (ON CLUSTER) ran with these restricted grants in
                 scratch report8; which user the replica-side DDL ran as is not shown (README item 38). Networks stay HOST LOCAL and the password stays
                 empty. Residual: through remote() the writer can act as default, which gives SELECT and INSERT on the six signoz_*
                 databases and SELECT on system.*, no more than the writer already has on those databases. -->
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_traces.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_metrics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_metadata.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_meter.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON signoz_analytics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON system.*</query>
            </grants>
        </default>
        <geldar_writer>
            <password_sha256_hex from_env="GELDAR_CH_WRITER_SHA256"/>
            <profile>geldar_writer</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <!-- [AUTH] Authored, not verified as minimal. The migrator passed with this list (scratch report8); a missing privilege fails with an
                 error that names it. Not granted on purpose: SYSTEM, FILE,
                 URL, S3, MYSQL, POSTGRES, SOURCES, KILL QUERY, dictGet, INTROSPECTION. CREATE DATABASE is not granted on *.*;
                 the CREATE grants below are on the six signoz_* databases only. CREATE on a database covers CREATE TABLE, CREATE VIEW
                 (materialized views) and CREATE DICTIONARY, so no separate VIEW grant is listed. ALTER covers ALTER UPDATE (the migration
                 status mutation). Table engines are granted one query each, because the Distributed engine's source is REMOTE.
                 REMOTE gives the writer the remote() and cluster() table functions to any host reachable from geldar-ch. That network
                 is shared with geldar-gateway, so it is not private. Observed in report8: through remote() the writer runs as default. Through remote() the writer can also act as default (see the
                 default block). The writer's password is held only by the migrator and the collector. Whether REMOTE is needed for
                 the Distributed engine is not tested apart from the other grants (README unverified list). [AUTH] -->
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_traces.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_metrics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_metadata.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_meter.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT, INSERT, ALTER, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, OPTIMIZE, SHOW ON signoz_analytics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON system.*</query>
                <query>GRANT CLUSTER ON *.*</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON Distributed</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON ReplicatedMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON ReplicatedReplacingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON ReplicatedAggregatingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON ReplicatedSummingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON MergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON ReplacingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON AggregatingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT TABLE ENGINE ON SummingMergeTree</query>
                <query>GRANT REMOTE ON *.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SHOW ON *.*</query>
            </grants>
            <networks>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
        </geldar_writer>
        <geldar_reader>
            <password_sha256_hex from_env="GELDAR_CH_READER_SHA256"/>
            <profile>geldar_reader</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_traces.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_metrics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_metadata.*</query>
            </grants>
            <networks>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
        </geldar_reader>
        <!-- [AUTH] D3: retention user (0370, ruled by geldar-93 on 2026-11-16 as "temporary override accepted"). SigNoz sets retention
             through POST /api/v1/settings/ttl, which runs ALTER TABLE ... ON CLUSTER ... MODIFY TTL over SigNoz's own ClickHouse
             connection. geldar_reader is readonly=2 and cannot run DDL, and it is NOT widened. This user is used only during a
             retention window through deploy/telemetry/compose.retention.yml, which swaps SigNoz's DSN to it; the override is removed
             afterwards (README, "Retention window (N6c)"). Its hash comes from GELDAR_CH_SIGNOZ_ADMIN_SHA256 in ch-hashes.env; with
             the variable unset geldar-ch REFUSES to start ("Env variable is not set"), so the hash goes into ch-hashes.env BEFORE
             this file reaches the node (README ordering).
             Grants are explicit and nothing else sits next to them (no access_management keys: they cannot coexist with grants;
             the stock keys apply only to default). ALTER TTL is the ClickHouse privilege (alias ALTER MODIFY TTL). Round 9
             (single replica, single shard) logged only is_initial_query = 1 rows, so it does not show which user the
             replica-side DDL ran as; it shows that ON CLUSTER MODIFY TTL succeeded for this user while default, the cluster
             entry's user, has no ALTER grants. Behaviour on other replicas is not shown (README item 38). The Distributed tables are altered too, and
             the grant is on whole databases so both are covered. SELECT on the three
             databases and on system.* because SigNoz reads engine_full from system.tables for the TTL status call; system.*
             is wider than system.tables, narrowing is untested [UNV]. CLUSTER is for ON CLUSTER.
             Ruled in scratch round 9: the logs v2 call (POST /api/v2/settings/ttl, type logs) runs ALTER TABLE signoz_logs.logs_v2 ON
             CLUSTER ... MODIFY COLUMN _retention_days and was refused with Code 497, so GRANT ALTER MODIFY COLUMN ON signoz_logs.* is
             added (narrow: signoz_logs only; it is the child of ALTER COLUMN that the error names). Traces and metrics need only ALTER
             TTL, as before. Existing rows keep their old _retention_days: v2 changes only the column default for new rows, and no
             materialization (ALTER UPDATE) is granted. Acceptable because nothing is ingested yet.
             NOT granted: INSERT, CREATE, DROP, TRUNCATE, SYSTEM, REMOTE, SOURCES, TABLE ENGINE, access management, ALTER UPDATE,
             ALTER DELETE, ALTER COLUMN on other databases, ALTER of settings. No grants on signoz_metadata, signoz_meter or
             signoz_analytics: whether the retention call touches them is not known [UNV]; the ALTER failure names the missing
             privilege. Cold storage needs ALTER MODIFY SETTING; unused here [UNV].
             Networks are all, as for the writer and the reader: the container reaches geldar-ch by name on the query network
             (geldar-telemetry-query); nothing is published. -->
        <geldar_signoz_admin>
            <password_sha256_hex from_env="GELDAR_CH_SIGNOZ_ADMIN_SHA256"/>
            <profile>geldar_signoz_admin</profile>
            <quota>default</quota>
            <grants>
                <query>GRANT ALTER TTL ON signoz_traces.*</query>
                <query>GRANT ALTER TTL ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT ALTER TTL ON signoz_metrics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT ALTER MODIFY COLUMN ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_traces.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_logs.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON signoz_metrics.*</query>
                <query>GRANT SELECT ON system.*</query>
                <query>GRANT CLUSTER ON *.*</query>
            </grants>
            <networks>
                <ip>::/0</ip>
            </networks>
        </geldar_signoz_admin>
    </users>
</clickhouse>
